  "id": "f839ea9d-76c6-569c-ae7a-5bad47795e66",
  "slug": "lasagna-roll-ups-ii",
  "name": "Lasagna Roll-Ups",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "A fun lasagna roll-ups recipe. Roll the traditional ingredients of sauce, ricotta blend, and mozzarella into noodles for an Italian-inspired dinner.",
  "cuisine": "Italian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Cook and stir ground beef, onion, garlic powder, and oregano in a large skillet over medium heat until onion is tender and beef is browned, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add tomato sauce and sugar; simmer until sauce is heated through, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook lasagna in the boiling water, stirring occasionally until cooked through but firm to the bite, 8 to 10 minutes. Drain."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Grease a 9x13-inch casserole dish."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Mix ricotta cheese, egg, parsley, and 3/4 cup Parmesan cheese together in a bowl."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Place a lasagna noodle on a work surface. Spoon one layer ricotta cheese mixture, one layer meat sauce, and one layer mozzarella cheese atop lasagna noodle; top with another lasagna noodle. Roll up the stuffed lasagna noodles in the jelly-roll style; place in the prepared casserole dish. Repeat with remaining lasagna noodles, ricotta cheese mixture, meat sauce, and mozzarella cheese."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Spread a spoonful of meat sauce atop each lasagna roll; top with remaining mozzarella cheese and 1/4 cup Parmesan cheese."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until cheese is melted and bubbling, 30 to 35 minutes."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 9,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 50,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 30,
